      "writtenOn": "2026-10-22T10:02:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "env.get() leaves LD_PRELOAD in the environment.\n\nwe could replace it with env.pop(\"LD_PRELOAD\", None) and that way sh and stdbuf don\u0027t see our preloads at all, but the app gets \"vcl:libstdbuf\" as intended. I\u0027ve no idea what rust uutils stdbuf does internally, but because src/vcl/ldp.c defines a bunch of libc wrapper functions (like read, close, write, poll, ...), I\u0027d rather be safe than sorry by NOT exposing these to the new uutils.",
      "revId": "a6079e763d536cd4fa2b0be3ee312b9425eb3d36",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
